Supply-temperature value (estimates per gap-cost report: US$0.8-2.0 M capex per K per 100 MW of dry cooler, US$0.16-0.32 M/yr per K trim-chiller energy in hot climates):
- GPU-class lidded (Rubin 2.3 kW, max dT gain, T1 PCM): +3.1 K supply at equal Tcase,max -> US$2.5-6.2 M capex + US$0.50-1.00 M/yr (hot climate) per 100 MW
- 15 kW-class conservative (P90): +9.2 K supply at equal Tcase,max -> US$7.4-18.4 M capex + US$1.47-2.94 M/yr (hot climate) per 100 MW
- 15 kW-class nominal T1: +13.1 K supply at equal Tcase,max -> US$10.5-26.2 M capex + US$2.10-4.19 M/yr (hot climate) per 100 MW
- 15 kW-class T2 LM: +19.2 K supply at equal Tcase,max -> US$15.4-38.4 M capex + US$3.07-6.14 M/yr (hot climate) per 100 MW

## 10. GPU-class tray loop (4 x 2.3 kW GPU + 2 x 0.5 kW CPU = 10.2 kW, 1.0 LPM/kW = 10.2 LPM)

- GPU plate (LoopCore-G, 60 cm2, 2.3 LPM): 2.7 kPa port-to-port
- per-plate branch with UQD04-class service pair: 11-24 kPa; with UQD06-class: 4-6 kPa
- tray UQDB08 pair at 10.2 LPM: 6.3-11.2 kPa; TFM orifice 10 kPa; cartridge+wells 0.3 kPa
- tray total (UQD04 service pairs): 28-45 kPa; (UQD06 service pairs): 21-28 kPa
- reference: vendor GB300-class skived plate 12 kPa at 1.7 LPM -> ~19 kPa at 2.3 LPM (flow^1.5), no service coupling; tray total 26-31 kPa without metering

